        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Isomorphous Ni6Dy6 cage 2 is not an SMM. Room-temperature χMT is 93.6 emu K mol−1 (calcd 92.3). χT decreases to 85.4 emu K mol−1 at 12 K then rises slightly to 85.9 emu K mol−1 at 7 K, attributed to DyIII crystal-field effects. Magnetization reaches 45.3 μB at 7 T and 2 K without saturation. −ΔSm = 12.2 J kg−1 K−1 at 3 K for ΔH = 70 kG, well below the 33.8 J kg−1 K−1 maximum because of NiII/DyIII anisotropy; the −ΔSm maximum shifts to higher temperature than for 1.",
