        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Diamagnetic-Y analogue 3 probes Ni···Ni coupling in two non-interacting {Ni3} triangles. Room-temperature χMT is 7.9 emu K mol−1 (calcd 7.3 for six S = 1, g = 2.2). χT rises to 10.6 emu K mol−1 at 8 K then falls to 8.0 emu K mol−1 at 2 K. MAGPACK fit of Hamiltonian (1) gives J1 = 2.83 cm−1, J2 = −1.18 cm−1, D = 5.7 cm−1, g = 2.28. No slow relaxation to 1.8 K. Smallest MCE of the series: −ΔSm = 5.6 J kg−1 K−1 at 3 K for ΔH = 70 kG (maximum 14.3 J kg−1 K−1).",
